Write the generated configuration in a fixed order.

The build script collects the configuration constants in a HashMap
and writes config.rs in the map's iteration order, which changes on
every run. The constants are the same, but the bytes of config.rs are
not, so each build of smoltcp has a different crate hash. A build on
one host then does not link against a crate that another host built
against its own copy, and the build stops with E0463 or E0460. A
BTreeMap writes the constants in name order on every run. Upstream
made the same change after 0.13.1.

Applies to smoltcp 0.13.1 from crates.io; the pin and this patch are
consumed by nix/patched-crates.nix.

--- a/build.rs
+++ b/build.rs
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-use std::collections::HashMap;
+use std::collections::BTreeMap;
 use std::fmt::Write;
 use std::path::PathBuf;
 use std::{env, fs};
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
         println!("cargo:rerun-if-env-changed=SMOLTCP_{name}");
     }
 
-    let mut configs = HashMap::new();
+    let mut configs = BTreeMap::new();
     for (name, default) in CONFIGS {
         configs.insert(
             *name,
